{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/858921-is-it-not-possible-to-transcend-the-5th-level-as-a-changing-breed","id":858921,"title":"Is it not possible to transcend the 5th level as a changing breed?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-04T05:52:33-07:00","id":858921,"title":"Is it not possible to transcend the 5th level as a changing breed?","content":"When vampires are 7th gen, Kuei-jin are at the 6th level of their chosen dharma, mages whenever they want to... They can reach beyond the limits of their human form in their human form. We're not talking about how technically a vampire has potence 5 so really that 13th gen is at 10 strength (well, that comes in to play) but rather that Mr Enlightened there has seven points of melee and therefore makes an expert look like a noob.<br /> <br /> Now, maybe it's because renown is an inherently greedy thing, and the changing cultures are poor as shit, or gaia put limitations on her servants, or she saw how vampires and Kuei-Jin were going and thought 'Nope, None of that' (Changing breeds mostly predate Cainites, so I'm not sure about this)<br /> <br /> Maybe it's because they don't live too long (well, Rokea live long, but for every 5 years spent learning they spend another 600 moving forward) (Kitsune sound like they should advance into post 5 with the tails, but I've found no rules on it.)<br /> <br /> Now, some totems can bring one beyond 6 in an attribute, but this is borrowed power, and although I have read that a ridiculous level of devotion to a totem might get you more from it, it's not a permanent or personal improvement.<br /> <br /> On the otherhand, some gifts basically are just improvements. The Cecillian have one that provides 3 dice to any instrument they play. I'm sure that somewhere I read that there was a gift that gave an extra die to all charisma rolls (forgot the name, but sure it's in there). King fish/Majesty adds one to all intimidation/leadership rolls. There's a few more.<br /> <br /> Another thing is that the gifts of the changers allow for superhuman levels of a skill, and could we therenot justify having more than five dots to something as these gifts feel innate? For example, dexterity with improvements such as ballance,Catfeet,Hare'sLeap, rathead, flame dance. Perception with all those new non-human abilities, Charisma with many things, stealth with manythings, brawl with many things. Even just the regenerative properties of the garou is a good help for brawl, as constant regeneration ensures you can go further than the common person in a sparing match. It feels odd to have superhuman ability and be limited by five dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7244,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","user":"Innocent Flower","date":". 04-04-2016, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T12:06:59-07:00","id":859155,"title":"","content":"Rank 6 exists, the Bastet book had a few. The Gurahl are led by at least one Rank 6. Almost all of the breed books had or hinted at rank 6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T12:40:28-07:00","id":859172,"title":"","content":"There's no over-arching reasons beyond different games with different design goals.<br /> <br /> WtA has, for a long time, frontloaded &quot;bread and butter&quot; power (essentially the 6+ ratings equivalents), and gated off &quot;story&quot; powers. Higher ranking characters in WtA do have more experience, thus higher stats and more toys, but they've vastly expanded in their powers that allow them to effect major alterations in the course of events (often without distinct mechanics).<br /> <br /> This generally stems from WtA being the game most focused on the PCs starting as violent individuals growing into bigger characters from there. All of the PC character start off being able to easily kill humans even without investing much into combat; with only situations dictating why it's a bad idea to resort to such things. But Rank 1 PCs don't have a lot of power beyond beyond their personal abilities. The game focuses (to use werewolves as a core example) on growing from a grunt to someone that sees the big picture of the war and needs to gain the power to push large scale efforts towards how they feel is the best course of action.<br /> <br /> A lot of the other games are far less frontloaded this way, and characters are more likely to have a lot more &quot;story&quot; powers. Vampires get some nice automatic perks, but without investment/preparation their default package doesn't simple let them curbstomp humans. However they also start with much strong abilities such as the addictive nature of their blood which can be used to dozens of goals.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T13:22:35-07:00","id":859215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/858921-is-it-not-possible-to-transcend-the-5th-level-as-a-changing-breed?p=859155#post859155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rank 6 exists, the Bastet book had a few. The Gurahl are led by at least one Rank 6. Almost all of the breed books had or hinted at rank 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't refer to rank, I refer to power and ability. Attribute wise 1 dot is weak and 5 dot is peak human. Bar totem,shifting and some gifts (the occasional merit) you can't get past this. <br /> <br /> Vampires for example can get computers 6,7,8,9 and 10 through blood potency or enlightenement. 6th rank glass walker? Still can't get past 5 computers (even If Cockroach and net spider are assisting) <br /> <br /> A vampire can have 8 strength (no potence) in human form. A werewolf can get that, but only through gifts and powers which take one out of human form or are very short lived. <br /> A werewolf simply can't do that in human form, they can use gifts and totems to temporarily reach the goal, but it isn't the same thing. They can get to four strength and crinos into 8, but they can't have 8 strength in homid which turns to 12. Why is it that only the vampires and mages can transend this ceiling, whilst the changing breeds are stuck to their earthly limits? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T13:30:25-07:00","id":859221,"title":"","content":"Mages cannot transcend that ceiling without the Legendary Attribute merit (which in theory might be available to the Garou). If they do transcend 5 it's either short term or they are prone to pattern bleed, which isn't very... nice.<br /> And if you're really keen on so much power, just sell your soul to the Wyrm. He's alwys been generous with powers (and tumors).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T13:33:18-07:00","id":859225,"title":"","content":"Because they aren't so invested on this, among other things due to their far more variable and versatile pick on supernatural powers?<br /> Honestly, it's not like a dice here or there is such a huge deal after some level, trick options get far more important than dots per se.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T13:44:10-07:00","id":859234,"title":"","content":"Isn't that what shifting form is for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T15:01:17-07:00","id":859274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/858921-is-it-not-possible-to-transcend-the-5th-level-as-a-changing-breed?p=859215#post859215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires for example can get computers 6,7,8,9 and 10 through blood potency or enlightenement. 6th rank glass walker? Still can't get past 5 computers (even If Cockroach and net spider are assisting)</div> </div> </div> </div>What does having Computers 6 get them that all of their Rank 1-6 Gifts doesn't?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A vampire can have 8 strength (no potence) in human form. A werewolf can get that, but only through gifts and powers which take one out of human form or are very short lived. </div> </div> </div>Ok... but how many 5th Generation vampires do you have running around in your games?<br /> <br /> Compare that to the fact that ever Garou on earth has the potential to get to Strength 7 just for shifting into Glabro and having Strength 5. Glabro isn't going to be a walking around form without extra powers/that one Merit, but you can certainly get away with using it with preparations.<br /> <br /> As well, looking human, and actually using Strength 8 to its full capacity is going to mark a vampire as not-human. Looking like a muscle bound giant brute and doing higher than human Strength is much less difficult for people to rationalize as you just being freakishly strong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why is it that only the vampires and mages can transend this ceiling, whilst the changing breeds are stuck to their earthly limits? </div> </div> </div>Consider (on top of everything else people are sayin) that the vampires and mages noted as doing so are also often centuries old. The potential for vampires and mages to do so, doesn't mean it is common place, easy, or something they are all capable of actually realizing. Garou don't live to be 500 years old to finally have achieved a state of enlightenment that allows them to finally get to 6 dots in Attributse/Skills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/858921-is-it-not-possible-to-transcend-the-5th-level-as-a-changing-breed?p=859221#post859221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages cannot transcend that ceiling without the Legendary Attribute merit (which in theory might be available to the Garou). If they do transcend 5 it's either short term or they are prone to pattern bleed, which isn't very... nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>While a lot of people (including the current M20 lead developer) don't like the books that touch on it, there are official rules for allowing Arete 6+ mages to increase their cap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T15:11:06-07:00","id":859281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/858921-is-it-not-possible-to-transcend-the-5th-level-as-a-changing-breed?p=859274#post859274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While a lot of people (including the current M20 lead developer) don't like the books that touch on it, there are official rules for allowing Arete 6+ mages to increase their cap.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know you know the backstory with that... But for the benefit of the others, the crux of the matter is that according to Brucatto there never was supposed to be a sphere rating of 6, it was a typo in Porthoses writeup in the Book of Chantries, and people were convinced it was a thing, to the point that there was popular and editorial demand to bring in the extra levels of the spheres. Brucatto brought in 6 as the ultimate ultimate sphere. Then after he left (but before they settled on the tone of Revised and the ideas therein) Brooks added a whole pile of extra spheres for reasons probably only known to her and WW editorial.<br /> <br /> One of the problems inherit in the Archspheres and tying the archepheres with the attributes is that it's a downright weird concept that doesn't really tie into the Spheres prior to the level 6. The bonus question is that if there are spheres beyond 6 why don't Voormas and Porthos have them? Add to that the confusion between which system of Archspheres you should use, or if they even exist (revised and now M20 are fuzzy on the concept)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T16:50:26-07:00","id":859325,"title":"","content":"This situation sounds like it needs Mummy-like supplemental effects for Attributes at 6+ to hammer the differences from Vampire home. Fear the Dexterity 9 of the Ratkin as nothing else! You won't even see them coming!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T15:53:18-07:00","id":860610,"title":"","content":"I don't think spreading Mummy-style Attribute twinkiness to more games is a solution to anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T16:27:24-07:00","id":860631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/858921-is-it-not-possible-to-transcend-the-5th-level-as-a-changing-breed?p=860610#post860610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think spreading Mummy-style Attribute twinkiness to more games is a solution to anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not twinkiness if everyone at the table has it. Provided they're playing the same game, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T19:56:59-07:00","id":860736,"title":"","content":"How different supernaturals get to 6+ in Attributes - and the potential costs thereof - doesn't make it an even field.<br /> <br /> As well, how do you handle the fact that the boosts from Mummy's 6+ are supposed to be like super-Specialties that don't apply to all uses of the Attribute?<br /> <br /> If a vampire blood buffs their Strength to 6, what determines the boost they get? Can they switch each scene they opt to do this based on what their intent is?<br /> <br /> How does this interact with supernatural powers? To stick with vampires here, if a character has base Dexterity 5, blood boosts to Dex 6, and has Celerity 2, do they get the Dex 6 MtC boost, or the Dex 8 one? Do the bonus extra actions MtC Dex 6+ grant stack with Celerity extra actions, or only work if you don't use Celerity extra actions (which is also very relevant to WtA via Rage)?<br /> <br /> You also have mages, who can boost all of their Attributes to 6+ via magic at starting level (if with lots of paradox issues), while vampires and werewolves only have innate boosts to their physical ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T20:15:56-07:00","id":860746,"title":"","content":"To clarify my suggestion: not Mummy's exact effects, just utilize the concept to make higher Attributes gained in other forms more significant than just adding more dice. Thus, we can avoid more extra actions from having Dex 6+ in forms other than Homid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T02:04:50-07:00","id":860881,"title":"","content":"That only addresses a very small part of what I said.<br /> <br /> There's two essential point that even with clarification the suggestion doesn't address:<br /> <br /> 1) What effects do they get? What's the determination? Is a selection permanent? How do those effects interact with powers even if you cut out something direct like multiple actions via Dex 6+? <i>Lots</i> of the MtC style boosts are going to interact with the same widgets as Disciplines/Gifts/etc.<br /> <br /> 2) How do you maintain the lack of &quot;twinkiness,&quot; when there's an uneven distribution of access to 6+ Attributes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T20:09:50-07:00","id":861555,"title":"","content":"Any starting werewolf can be Strength 9 by changing forms...<br /> <br /> If anything, that puts Werewolves as the twinkiest in a purely physical contest.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T16:08:41-07:00","id":862246,"title":"","content":"I've always thought form-enhanced Stamina to soak aggravated damage and the ease of regaining Rage after spending it on extra attacks contribute far more to overpowered werewolves than the enhanced strength. A 500 lb. supernatural creature whose muscles are based on a wolf's <i>should</i> be as strong as several athletic human beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}